<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
     Local manifest for malbec (Lenovo TB390FU) on LineageOS 23.2.

     Copy to .repo/local_manifests/malbec.xml in a fresh checkout, then
     `repo sync`.

     ⚠️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS INSTEAD OF `breakfast malbec`

     `lineage.dependencies` is the LineageOS-native mechanism and it CANNOT work
     for a personal fork. vendor/lineage/build/tools/roomservice.py hardcodes the
     LineageOS organisation in two places:

         line 222   'name': f'LineageOS/{repo_name}'
         line 327   git ls-remote https://:@github.com/LineageOS/<repo_name>

     and the `remote` escape at lines 226 to 233 applies only to `aosp-*`
     remotes; for anything else it sets project.remote and leaves the
     LineageOS-prefixed name in place. So a dependency written as

         "repository": "suddenBook/proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec"

     is probed as `LineageOS/suddenBook/proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec`, comes
     back with no branches, and roomservice.py line 349 exits with

         Default revision lineage-23.2 not found in ... Bailing.

     Moving the three repos onto the `lineage-23.2` branch was a real and
     separate bug, and fixing it was necessary but not sufficient: the
     organisation prefix cannot be fixed from the device tree at all. Hence this
     file.

     `lineage.dependencies` is kept as it is. It is correct, and it starts
     working the day these repos live under LineageOS.

     ⚠️ AFTER SYNCING, BEFORE BUILDING

     TWO repositories here use Git LFS and `repo sync` does not smudge it.

       vendor/lenovo/malbec   libarcsoft_faceid.so, 134 MB — above GitHub's
                              per-file limit. Left un-smudged it is a 134-byte
                              text file and the build stops with "must have a
                              valid ELF magic word", which reads like a corrupt
                              blob rather than a missing object.
       vendor/gapps           GmsCore.apk (175 MB) and Velvet.apk (254 MB).
                              Left un-smudged, GMS builds "successfully" and the
                              device has no Play Services at all.

     In BOTH, run the two LFS commands from the device tree's README
     (`git lfs install` with the local flag, then `git lfs pull`). `git lfs pull`
     on its own prints "Skipping object checkout, Git LFS is not installed for
     this repository" and EXITS 0. work/scripts/01-lfs-check.sh is tree-wide and
     is a pre-flight in 40-build.sh, so a build cannot start with a pointer.

     ⚠️ ABOUT vendor/gapps

     This device ships full GMS (owner's decision, session 23). LineageOS's own
     mechanism — WITH_GMS=true plus vendor/partner_gms — is not usable outside
     the official build farm: partner_gms is not in the public manifest and
     LineageOS/android_vendor_partner_gms is not a public repository. MindTheGapps
     is the maintained public equivalent; branch `baklava` is Android 16, which
     is what LineageOS 23.x is. It MUST be checked out at exactly `vendor/gapps`:
     its common-vendor.mk inherits `vendor/gapps/common/common-vendor.mk` by
     absolute path.

     The revision is pinned to a branch rather than a SHA deliberately — GMS
     needs to track Google's security updates — but that also means two syncs a
     month apart do not produce the same image. Pin a SHA here if you need a
     reproducible build.
-->
<manifest>
  <remote name="suddenBook"
          fetch="https://github.com/suddenBook"
          revision="refs/heads/lineage-23.2" />

  <project path="device/lenovo/malbec"
           name="android_device_lenovo_malbec"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <project path="device/lenovo/malbec-kernel"
           name="android_device_lenovo_malbec-kernel"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <project path="vendor/lenovo/malbec"
           name="proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <!--
       ⚠️ FRAMEWORKS/BASE IS FORKED, AND THIS IS THE ONLY THING THAT SAYS SO.

       The parallel-window feature (系统级平行视界 — a phone-only app laid out
       as two panes) cannot be built from a device tree. It needs five changes
       inside frameworks/base, and no amount of overlay, property or prebuilt
       reaches any of them:

         ActivityThread              loads androidx.window.extensions into app
                                     processes that do not declare it — measured,
                                     131 of 178 packages on this device do not
         WindowOrganizerController   lets a rule-covered package past the
                                     non-resizeable owner-activity gate
         ActivityRecord              suppresses the relaunch a split transition
                                     would otherwise cause
         IActivityTaskManager        one @hide method, uid-authenticated
         wm/parallelwindow/          the rule store itself

       The fork is LineageOS/android_frameworks_base with one topic commit on
       top of lineage-23.2. It is NOT a divergent branch — rebasing it onto a
       newer lineage-23.2 is a normal `git pull --rebase`, and the whole delta
       is +224 lines in seven existing files plus six new ones.

       ★ WITHOUT THIS ENTRY the checkout silently gets upstream's frameworks/base
       and the feature vanishes with no build error and no boot failure: apps
       launch, nothing splits. work/scripts/52-parallel-window.py exists because
       every supply chain in this feature fails exactly that quietly.
  -->
  <remove-project name="LineageOS/android_frameworks_base" />

  <project path="frameworks/base"
           name="android_frameworks_base"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <remote name="mindthegapps"
          fetch="https://gitlab.com/MindTheGapps" />

  <project path="vendor/gapps"
           name="vendor_gapps"
           remote="mindthegapps"
           revision="baklava"
           clone-depth="1" />
</manifest>
